Find the largest logit on the backend when every slot samples greedily.

A decode read all the logits back from the GPU, 107520 floats per sequence for PLaMo 3
Translate, and the greedy path of 0011 then scanned them for one index. When every slot that
samples from the next decode can only take the largest logit, the graph now ends in an argmax
node and only those indices are read back. Any other request, and a model whose output layer
is on the CPU, keeps the logits.

The WebGPU argmax shader returned the highest index among equal values, and -1 for a row with
nothing above its floor. It now returns the lowest index, as the scan does, and never -1.

